RECEIPT 01 — SHINYHUNTERS SPEAKS FIRST

Before Medtronic publicly confirmed the incident, ShinyHunters listed the company and claimed to possess:

9M+ records

plus large volumes of corporate information.

A reported extortion deadline was set for April 21.

Classification

THREAT-ACTOR CLAIM

Not:

COMPANY-CONFIRMED SCALE

That distinction must remain visible forever in SecurityReceipts.

RECEIPT 02 — MEDTRONIC CONFIRMS ACCESS

On April 24, Medtronic publicly confirmed that an unauthorized party accessed data in certain corporate IT systems.

That transforms:

ATTACKER CLAIM

into:

CONFIRMED INCIDENT

but it does not automatically validate every attacker claim.

InfinityGrid classification:

INCIDENT — CONFIRMED

9M COUNT — UNVERIFIED

SHINYHUNTERS ATTRIBUTION — CLAIMED

