CRITICAL BREACH
≠
CRITICAL OUTAGE
PATIENT SAFETY ≠ PATIENT PRIVACY

This case gives InfinityGrid a very sharp distinction.

Medtronic says:

patient safety was not affected.

That does not mean:

patients were not affected.

Compare:

PATIENT SAFETY
=
Can the device safely deliver therapy?

versus:

PATIENT PRIVACY
=
Was sensitive information exposed?

A company can succeed at one while failing at the other.

That's exactly what appears to have happened here.

